on": {"value": 1.2, "source": "extension", "hidden": ""}, "Categories": {"value": "Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Quality images of the United States|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Featured pictures of the United States|Taken with Canon EOS 5D Mark IV|Taken with Sigma 20mm F1.4 DG HSM Art|Photographs with aspect ratio of 3:2|ISO speed rating 200|Self-published work|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/United States|Featured pictures of Yellowstone National Park|Exposure time 1/250 sec|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Featured pictures|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Quality images|Information field template with formatting|National Register of Historic Places with known IDs|Featured pictures on Wikipedia, Vietnamese|Lens focal length 20 mm|June 2022 in Wyoming|Images by XRay (flat list)|Protected areas with known WDPA-ID|Uploaded with LrMediaWiki|Featured pictures of lakes|F-number f/13|United States photographs taken on 2022-06-22|Springs in 2022|Blue sky in Wyoming|Sulfur compounds at the Yellowstone Caldera|Volcanic degassing in 2022|Featured pictures of landscapes in the United States|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Landscape photography|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Featured pictures on Wikimedia Commons|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Quality images of lakes|Bacterial mats|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Featured pictures on Wikipedia|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Quality images of World Heritage Sites|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Quality images of national parks|Views of Grand Prismatic Spring|Grand Prismatic Spring degassing in 2022|Thermophile bacteria at Grand Prismatic Spring|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Quality images of volcanism|Photographs by Dietmar Rabich/Year/2022|Acidic lakes of the Yellowstone Caldera in 2022", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "Assessments": {"value": "quality|featured|potd", "source": "commons-categories", "hidden": ""}, "GPSLatitude": {"value": "44.525113", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "GPSLongitude": {"value": "-110.838198", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "GPSMapDatum": {"value": "WGS-84", "source": "commons-desc-page", "hidden": ""}, "ImageDescription": {"value": "<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grand_Prismatic_Spring\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Grand Prismatic Spring\">Grand Prismatic Spring</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellowstone_National_Park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Yellowstone National Park\">Yellowstone National Park</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wyoming\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Wyoming\">Wyoming</a>, USA<br><small>Yellowstone <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_park\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:National park\">National Park</a> was founded on March 1, 1872, and is considered the world’s first national park. It is located primarily in the state of Wyoming, but also extends into <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Montana\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Montana\">Montana</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idaho\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Idaho\">Idaho</a>. The initiative to establish the park was based on scientific expeditions from 1869 to 1871, which documented the unique landscape. President Ulysses S. Grant signed the protection law.<br>The park covers approximately 8,983 km² and is located on a massive volcanic hotspot. About half of all geysers worldwide are found here. The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Faithful\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"en:Old Faithful\">Old Faithful</a> geyser, which erupts approximately every 90 minutes, is famous. In addition to geysers, hot springs, mud pots, and the colorful Grand Prismatic Spring characterize the area.<br>Yellowstone is also an important wildlife refuge. Since the reintroduction of wolves in 1995, it has been considered a model project for nature conservation. The park attracts several million visitors annually and has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1978.</small>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "DateTimeOriginal": {"value": "Taken on 22 June 2022, 12:29", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Credit": {"value": "<span class=\"int-own-work\" lang=\"en\">Own work</span>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Artist": {"value": "<bdi><a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q34788025\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q34788025\"><span title=\"German photographer and mathematician\">Dietmar Rabich</span></a></bdi>", "source": "commons-desc-page"}, "Permission": {"value": "<table class=\"layouttemplate navigation-not-searchable\" style=\"margin:.25em;padding:.25em .5em;background-color:var(--background-color-base,#ffffff);color:inherit;border:1px solid var(--background-color-disabled,#eeeeee)\" data-nosnippet=\"\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Flag_of_Germany.svg/40px-Flag_of_Germany.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"24\" height=\"14\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Flag_of_Germany.svg/60px-Flag_of_Germany.svg.png?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1000\" data-file-height=\"600\"></span></span>\n</td>\n<td>Dieser Text und viele andere auch sind ebenso in deutscher Sprache verfügbar. Um diese sehen zu können, wähle bitte auf dieser Webseite die Spracheinstellung „Deutsch“.\n</td></tr></tbody></table><div style=\"clear:both;border:1px solid var(--background-color-disabled,#eeeeee);margin:.25em;padding:.25em .5em;background-color:var(--background-color-base,#ffffff);color:inherit;font-size:90%;\" class=\"searchaux\" data-nosnippet=\"\">\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HSSection_sign.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/HSSection_sign.svg/120px-HSSection_sign.svg.png?utm_s